The '''Secretary General of the Secretariat Council''' ({{lang-bl|Secretario General del Consejo de la Secretaría}}), often shortened to '''SG''' or '''SecGen''', and known in [[W:English language|Trent]] as the '''Premier''' or '''Prime Minister''' of [[Balisca]], is the chair of the [[Secretariat Council (Balisca)|Secretariat Council]]. The Secretary General is considered to be {{W|Primus inter pares|"first among equals"}} of the Council, and is representative of the confederal-level administration in [[Balisca]]. 

The Secretary General is elected directly by the people to serve for three years, but has no term limits. Pursuant to the provisions of the Constitution, the Secretary General must be elected by an [[W:Absolute majority|absolute majority]]. If no candidate succeeds in passing this threshold in the first round of counting, each following round eliminates the candidate with the fewest [[W:First-preference vote|first-preferences]] (among the remaining candidates) and transfers their votes if possible. This continues until one candidate accumulates a majority of the votes still in play. 

In order to be registered as a candidate in the premiership election, one must be a Baliscan citizen, be at least 18 years old on the day of the first round of the election, and must be a [[Commune district|congressional delegate]].

